# No unnecessary shell

Do not use the Shell tool by default. It is not for reading, searching, listing, or answering.

Use Read, Grep, and Glob for the repo. If the user asked a question you can answer, answer it. Do not run a command first.

Shell is allowed only when something must execute: a build, tests, git (when asked), the relaunch-after-build command, or an install the task requires.

If a command would only prompt the user to approve a look-around, do not run it.
